            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0318" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/5326</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Finnish Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Aström</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-27">November 27, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to refer to Your
                    Excellency’s note, dated October 27 [<hi rendition="#italic">24</hi>], 1931, by
                    which you were good enough to inform me about the proposal set forth by the
                    President of the United States in his statement of June 20, 1931, concerning the
                    postponement of payments upon the debts of foreign governments to the American
                    government during the fiscal year beginning July 1, 1931.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inform Your Excellency that my Government has now instructed
                    me to state that it is glad to accept the proposal made by the President of the
                    United States, referred to above.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. Aström</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
